From: Tyler South <tsouth2@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:41:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Link the shared folder into the home directory under its own
 name

The launcher names its -Share folder on the kernel command line
(tryomarchy.sharename, base64). A per-login user unit links ~/<name> to
/mnt/host, removes the link on launches that share nothing, and never
replaces a real folder with content.
---
 .../try-omarchy-share-link.service            |  1 +
 .../user/try-omarchy-share-link.service       | 13 ++++
 .../usr/local/lib/try-omarchy/share-link      | 69 +++++++++++++++++++
 guest/tests/verify.py                         | 11 +++
 4 files changed, 94 insertions(+)
 create mode 120000 guest/factory-overlay/etc/systemd/user/default.target.wants/try-omarchy-share-link.service
 create mode 100644 guest/factory-overlay/etc/systemd/user/try-omarchy-share-link.service
 create mode 100755 guest/factory-overlay/usr/local/lib/try-omarchy/share-link

diff --git a/guest/factory-overlay/etc/systemd/user/default.target.wants/try-omarchy-share-link.service b/guest/factory-overlay/etc/systemd/user/default.target.wants/try-omarchy-share-link.service
